This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Shard b of layer-readopt-gate runs unit e2: register-drift.sh in place over synthetic dist/cons worlds the fixture builds itself. The subject takes every world path as an argument and resolves its siblings from its own path, so its verdict is a function of its bytes and the world, not of where it is installed. A consumer runs the shipped shards a and c, which resolve readopt-override.sh, unregistered-drift.sh, register-drift.sh and layer-drift.sh in either layout and drive each in place.
